# Findings accepted with a reason and a date, not suppressed.
#
# The rule is the same one scripts/govulncheck-gate.sh follows: an exception
# exists only while the reasoning next to it holds, and it carries an expiry so
# it cannot quietly become permanent. Anything not listed here still fails the
# build.

# ── util-linux in the web-ui image — no fix available on this Alpine branch ───
#
# services/web-ui builds on nginx:1.30-alpine, which is Alpine 3.24. Trivy
# reports libuuid 2.42.1-r0 against a fix in 2.42.3-r0, and that package is not
# in the 3.24 repository yet: the runtime stage already runs `apk upgrade
# --no-cache` on every build — demonstrably working, since the same change took
# the Go images from an openssl HIGH to zero findings — and the version has not
# moved. There is nothing this repository can do until Alpine publishes it.
#
# What the seven CVEs are: privilege escalation through mount(8), nsenter and
# X-mount hooks. Reaching any of them requires running those programs. This
# container runs nginx as USER nginx, under no-new-privileges, and never mounts
# anything — so the vulnerable code is present in the filesystem and not
# reachable by anything the image executes.
#
# EXPIRES 2026-12-01. Past that date these stop being ignored and the build goes
# red again, which is the point: re-check whether 2.42.3-r0 has landed and
# delete this block rather than extending it out of habit.
CVE-2026-53612 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-53613 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-53614 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-76642 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-78408 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-78409 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-78410 exp:2026-12-01
